# S/MIME test fixtures are real `openssl smime` output, verified byte for
# byte before being committed (see meron-core/src/crypto/smime_tests.rs). The
# signatures inside them are over exact bytes, CRLF included where CRLF is
# what OpenSSL wrote — so nothing here may go through Git's line-ending
# normalization, on any platform, regardless of a checkout's core.autocrlf.
# `binary` is `-text -diff`: no conversion, and a byte diff of base64 CMS
# content would not be readable anyway.
/meron-core/src/crypto/testdata/** binary
# The pinned EasyPrivacy snapshot (#107): byte-for-byte as recorded in its
# README, so its hash holds on every checkout; not diffed line by line.
/meron-core/src/privacy/easyprivacy.txt binary
